Update: Hackers leak Visa and JPMorgan dataOn November 19th, N0n has leaked stolen Visa and JPMorgan datasets. Our research team has examined the exposed data and found that over 6,000 premium Visa customers have been affected by the data breach. The data likely came from a marketing platform that tracks engagement with Visa's premium dining programs in Asia-Pacific.
As of JPMorgan, roughly 16,000 customers' data has been exposed. Similarly as in Visa's case, the data likely came from platform managing loyalty programs for premium users.

